title ALES183 — Lotus's stereo_taps: the multi-tap delay carried into stereo, the SAME tap set on BOTH channels, each channel read off ITS OWN frozen dry snapshot — the second rung of the stereo TIME-BASED wing, the echo's snapshot sibling
prompt Autonomous loop lap after ALES182: recur through agent-doable work Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve the design round, send each finished increment to origin and xykj61 as its own signed round, STOP at custody gates.
think ALES181 opened the stereo time-based wing with the feedback echo and ALES182 gave it its real-time face. The wing's OTHER primitive is the multi-tap (ALES68) — several FIXED taps of the dry, independent early reflections that never feed each other, the discrete pattern a single feeding echo cannot voice. Lindy-first + crux-first: carrying it into stereo opens the wing's second lane and is the honest rung to take BEFORE the reverb (the wing's large composition, built from exactly these bounded early-reflection stages). It is also cleanly-tractable — a SNAPSHOT read (like vibrato ALES178, chorus ALES179), linear in the input, so its stereo carry preserves the panned integer ratio EXACTLY, the stronger both-cases image law the feedback echo could not earn.
think ALES68's multitap validated inline (private check_taps + range checks), so factored a pub precheck(clip_len, start, count, taps) out of it — additive, mirroring ALES66/71/72/73's own precheck refactors — and had multitap call it. Re-ran mono ales-taps GREEN (touches no buffer, reads a plain length). Composed stereo_taps mirroring the established pattern: StereoTapError = taps.TapError reused whole, validate ONCE against the shared length, then run taps.multitap per channel with the SAME tap set. Each channel snapshots and reads its OWN dry — no cross-channel snapshot, the mono discipline twice.
think Proved three laws: stereo multi-tap law (each channel == mono multitap byte for byte with genuinely different per-channel content, the channels differing so no crossing); dry-identity law (num=0 the exact dry master on both); image/balance/silence/atomicity/degenerate — and here the image law is the STRONGER both-cases one: an identical-channel master staying identical AND a panned pair kept off the rail keeping its exact ratio (right·2 == left, sample for sample), which the snapshot read earns and the feedback echo's @divTrunc truncation cannot. Four refusals (BadTapCount, BadDelay, BadLevel, BadRange) each leave both channels untouched and balanced, count 0 the identity.
obs No custody gate reached — pure local i16 DSP siloed to lotus/, a self-approved design round. Built and ran on metal; stereo_taps selftest GREEN through Rishi, mono ales-taps re-runs GREEN after the additive refactor, TAME style bans clean. The stereo time-based wing now holds BOTH its primitives (the feedback echo and the snapshot multi-tap); the reverb — built from bounded early-reflection stages — is the wing's large composition awaiting its turn, and a timed twin (stereo_multitap_ms) follows the stereo_echo_time pattern.
